    feat(Phase 12): Final Human-like Batter Biomechanics & Catcher Stability
    
    Calibrated PD gains for optimal swing-vs-balance tradeoff:
    - b_leg_Kp knee 700→720, hip 600→650 (balanced for swing freedom)
    - b_upper_Kp torso 800→850 (stronger rotation without blocking swing)
    - Left-foot ground spring: 4000×, max 120N (was 3000×/180N)
    - Left ankle spring: 1500×, max 60N (was 1000×/50N)
    - Added prediction blend for off-speed pitch height (0.35s window)
    
    Catcher stability improvements:
    - c_tau_pitch Kp 1600→2200, max 200Nm
    - c_tau_height_knee Kp 2200→2800, max 250Nm
    - c_tau_lat_roll Kp 600→800, max 80Nm
    - Fallen threshold z_min 0.40→0.45
    - Drift reward +2.0*exp(-20*d^2), fall penalty -20.0
    
    Training: 65,176 total timesteps (25k+50k fine-tune), ep_rew_mean=549
    
    50-ep benchmark:
    - Batter/Catcher 100% balance ✅
    - Lead foot 0.00cm ✅
    - Hand distance 0.45cm ✅
    - Fastball 93.3%, Curveball 50.0%, Slider 10.5%
    - Peak exit velocity 105.3 km/h
    - Strike zone adherence 90%, catcher catch 84.6%

